[Applause]  give me one minute and i'll show you  how virtual private cloud serves as a  foundation for your network in the cloud  virtual private cloud or vpc is the  managed networking service  for your google cloud infrastructure you  can think of it as  similar to a traditional physical  network except it's virtualized within  google cloud  vpcs on google cloud have a global scope  so a single vpc can span across multiple  regions  all over the world securely without  communicating across the public internet  vpcs are shareable between google cloud  projects  or even organizations in some cases that  means  you can use a single shared vpc for your  entire organization  so that teams isolated within projects  can maintain a shared private ip space  to access  commonly used services need to expand  your network  no problem google cloud vpc lets you  increase the iep space of any subnet  without any downtime  or workload shutdown giving you the  flexibility to grow your network to meet  your needs  by default your google cloud projects  are ready to roll with a default vpc  configured with multiple subnets created  across multiple regions  you can use these subnets or you can  create your own allowing you to  configure the number of subnets their  corresponding regions  and their ip address ranges do you have  existing infrastructure outside of  google cloud that you want to connect to  your vpc  there are multiple ways to create a  hybrid networking solution using  dedicated or partner interconnect  cloud vpn or even via partner supported  sd-wan connections  keep things on your network safe and  secure with packet mirroring  this allows you to mirror all traffic  between your compute instances  in your vpc so that you can inspect and  analyze it for application performance  issues  or to detect threats and anomalies so  next time you're looking into how you  can build your network in the cloud take  a minute to check out  google cloud vpcs or private managed  network in the cloud  to learn more check out cloud.google.com  vpc

